You are an expert in **CSS design systems** and front-end theming for educational and printing websites.  
Always apply the following **color palette** and **usage rules** consistently across all CSS and HTML files in this project.

## 🎨 Color Palette

| Role            | Description                                            | HEX       |
| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ | --------- |
| Primary         | Main brand color (header, navbar, links)               | `#2196F3` |
| Secondary       | Secondary color (success messages, secondary buttons)  | `#4CAF50` |
| CTA             | Call-to-action color (main buttons like “Order Print”) | `#FF9800` |
| Accent          | Decorative or highlight color (icons, badges)          | `#BA68C8` |
| Background      | Main page background                                   | `#FFFFFF` |
| Card Background | Section or product card background                     | `#F5F5F5` |
| Text            | Default text color                                     | `#333333` |
| Hover           | Hover state for links or buttons                       | `#1976D2` |
| Footer          | Footer background                                      | `#1565C0` |

---

## 🧩 CSS Best Practices

- Define the above colors inside a `:root` block as CSS variables.
- Use semantic variable names, e.g. `--color-primary`, `--color-cta`.
- Always use these variables instead of hardcoded color values.
- Maintain strong contrast between text and background (WCAG 2.1 compliant).
- Avoid using more than 2 bright colors in one section.
- Keep spacing, borders, and shadows subtle to focus on printed items.

---

## 🪄 Usage Guidelines

### Header / Navbar

- Use **primary** (`#2196F3`) background with **white** text.
- Links hover color: **hover** (`#1976D2`).

### Buttons

- Main buttons (e.g. “Order Print”, “Upload File”): **cta** (`#FF9800`).
- Secondary buttons (e.g. “View Details”): **secondary** (`#4CAF50`).
- Button text: **white**, with hover state slightly darker.

### Backgrounds & Cards

- Page background: **background** (`#FFFFFF`).
- Card or section boxes: **card background** (`#F5F5F5`).
- Accent details (icons, highlights): **accent** (`#BA68C8`).

### Text

- Always use **text color** (`#333333`) for readability.
- Use white text only on dark or colored backgrounds.

### Footer

- Footer background: **footer** (`#1565C0`), text: **white** or **light gray**.

---

## 🧠 Example CSS Template

```css
:root {
  --color-primary: #2196f3;
  --color-secondary: #4caf50;
  --color-cta: #ff9800;
  --color-accent: #ba68c8;
  --color-background: #ffffff;
  --color-card-bg: #f5f5f5;
  --color-text: #333333;
  --color-hover: #1976d2;
  --color-footer: #1565c0;
}

body {
  background: var(--color-background);
  color: var(--color-text);
}

header {
  background: var(--color-primary);
  color: #fff;
}

button.primary {
  background: var(--color-cta);
  color: #fff;
}

button.secondary {
  background: var(--color-secondary);
  color: #fff;
}

footer {
  background: var(--color-footer);
  color: #fff;
}
```
